# Assignments
.row gap:{1cm}
  .container width:{33%}
    .box title:{Assignment I (10%)}
      - Precipitation.
      - **Out now**, due Friday 21 August
      - _Analysing a precipitation record_.

  .container width:{33%}
    .box title:{Assignment II (15%)}
      - Total water storage.
      - Posted Week 5, due Friday 25 September
      - _Deriving soil moisture and groundwater change from GRACE space gravity_.

  .container width:{33%}
    .box title:{Assignment III (15%)}
      - Groundwater.
      - Posted Week 9, due Friday 23 October
      - _Analysing groundwater levels and storage_.
.fullspan
  .align{center}
    .container width:{60%}
      .box type:{note} background:{.lightred}
        - Assignments are posted on Canvas; the first one is already there, so you can start before we cover the lecture material.
        - The three assignments are worth 10%, 15% and 15% (40% in total).


# Paper Critique

.row gap:{1cm}
  .container width:{50%} borderwidth:{1px} padding:{0.5cm} radius:{0.1cm} background:{.lightblue}
    ## 1. Oral Presentation
    - Each student presents a selected paper (10-minute talk). (Chosen from a list of papers, first come first serve)
    - Presentations take place in Week 10.
    - Assessed by the instructor; worth 20% of the course.

  .container width:{50%} borderwidth:{1px} padding:{0.5cm} radius:{0.1cm} background:{rgb(200, 225, 200)}
    ## 2. Engagement
    - Attend the presentations.
    - Ask questions and take part in the discussion.



